<title>HONG KONG: CIBC CEF sets warrants on HK utilites stocks.</title>
<headline>CIBC CEF sets warrants on HK utilites stocks.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Canadian Imperial Bank of Commerce, London Branch, said on Tuesday it launched 280 million American-style call warrants on a basket of Hong Kong utilites stocks.</p>
<p>The basket comprises of:</p>
<p> China Light &amp; Power Co Ltd		    0.15 share</p>
<p> Hong Kong Telecommunications Ltd	    0.3  share</p>
<p>Ten warrants control one basket.</p>
<p> STRIKE PRICE	 HK$11.07225   PREMIUM	 11.6 PCT</p>
<p> ISSUE PRICE	  HK$0.1935     GEARING	 6.02x</p>
<p> EXPIRATION	   03.JUN.98     MIN EXER LOT  10,000</p>
<p> REFERENCE SPOT     HK$11.655     LISTING DATE  03.JUN.97</p>
<p> LISTING		HONG KONG</p>
<p> NOTE		   PHYSICAL OR CASH SETTLEMENT AT ISSUER'S</p>
<p>			  DISCRETION</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441.  http://www.hk97.com</p>
</text>
